From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maxim Stepanov <g.maxim.stepanoff@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 1 Jul 2026 02:21:04 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui: unify subagent titlebar chrome, fix list-height
 cache bug

Every focused_subagent toggle (the restored pop-out open button, the
back button, and the group-disclosure expand/collapse) now calls
ListState::reset(entry_count) before notifying, fixing the parent
transcript scroll corruption that occurred on first pop-out open
(GPUI's list.rs requires this when an off-screen item's height changes,
which a visibility-flip across many entries clearly is).

Also extracts the native subagent titlebar's visual chrome into a
shared render_subagent_titlebar_chrome helper so qwen's focused
breadcrumb is pixel-identical, generalizes is_entry_visible to cover
text entries and recursive nesting via the new SubagentIndex::
is_in_subtree_of (which, unlike root_of, does not short-circuit at a
nested root), and adds recursive nested-card dispatch in
render_subagent_expanded_content via children_of.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
